Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.5.1 card audit): the computer player attacks and blocks as a team.

Reason: XMage's AI declares its own attackers and blockers alone. In a team game (Game.getTeammates,
from part 1) its lethal-attack check now counts the attackers its teammate has declared or, when it
declares first (it holds the team's turn), could declare (805.10b), against the defending team's
blockers together (805.10d); a defending AI leaves alone the attackers its teammate has blocked; and
the poison part of the lethal check counts the defending team's counters against the format's number
(810.10, 810.8d: 15 in Two-Headed Giant) instead of a player's own against ten. Other games are
unchanged.
Needs parts 1 and 3 (Game.getPoisonCounters, getPoisonCountersToLose).
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage with the other parts.
Remove when: XMage upstream's AI supports teams, or Two-Headed Giant is dropped.

